## Proposed Changes

We will create/update the following Test suites in the `tests/Feature/` directory to cover your requirements.

### 1. Public Website & Redirections
- **`PublicWebsiteTest.php`**
  - [NEW] Test all public routes (`/`, `/about`, `/contact`, etc.) to ensure they return a 200 OK status.
  - [NEW] Verify that any outdated or protected links correctly redirect users (e.g., redirecting unauthenticated users to `/login`).

### 2. Lead Generation & Forms
- **`PublicLeadSubmissionTest.php`**
  - [NEW] Simulate submitting the Advertiser Enquiry form with valid/invalid data.
  - [NEW] Simulate submitting the Location Partner form.
  - [NEW] Assert that the leads are correctly saved in the database.
  - [NEW] Assert that an Admin user can view these exact leads in the Admin Panel Lead section.

### 3. Admin Profile Management
- **`AdminSettingsTest.php`**
  - [NEW] Test changing the Admin's username and saving it.
  - [NEW] Test updating the Admin's password with correct validation rules (matching confirmation, minimum length).
  - [NEW] Verify that the Admin can log back in with the newly updated password.

### 4. Admin Panel Core Functionalities
- **`AdminFullWorkflowTest.php`**
  - [NEW] Test creating new Location Partners and Advertisers as an Admin.
  - [NEW] Test adding a new Location and associating it with a Partner.
  - [NEW] Test updating existing Locations and approving Location Partner accounts.
  - [NEW] Re-verify the Campaign Workflow (from creation to approval to scheduling).

### 5. Multi-User Workflow Simulation
- **`MultiUserWorkflowTest.php`**
  - [NEW] Create 5 distinct Location Partners and 5 Advertisers programmatically.
  - [NEW] Simulate them logging into their respective panels simultaneously (using loops in the test).
  - [NEW] Simulate advertisers creating multiple campaigns across different locations.
  - [NEW] Simulate partners approving/viewing the screens.
  - [NEW] Monitor for any 500 errors or database lock exceptions during rapid data insertion to ensure the business workflow is perfectly solid.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
Once the tests are written, I will execute the entire test suite using:
- `php artisan test`

This will give us a complete pass/fail report on every single functionality in the system.

### Manual Verification
- After automated tests pass, I will spin up a browser subagent to visually verify the frontend lead form submission and admin panel visual updates to guarantee everything looks correct on the screen.
